= Solution
{parent=a}

Write the <partial fraction decomposition> as $A/(x-3)+B/(x+7)$. After multiplying through, $7x+29=A(x+7)+B(x-3)$. Setting $x=3$ gives $A=5$, and setting $x=-7$ gives $B=2$, so
$$
\boxed{\frac{7x+29}{(x-3)(x+7)}=\frac5{x-3}+\frac2{x+7},\qquad x\ne3,-7.}
$$

= b
{parent=7}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Use <completing the square> by adding and subtracting $3^2$:
$$
\boxed{x^2-6x+14=(x-3)^2+5.}
$$

