For $a>0$, write $a^x=e^{x\ln a}$ and apply the <chain rule>:
$$
\boxed{\frac d{dx}a^x=(\ln a)a^x.}
$$
This also covers $a=1$, for which both sides are zero.

= b
{parent=8}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=b}

Differentiate the outer <sine>, then the inner <cosine>. The <chain rule> gives
$$
\boxed{\frac d{dx}\sin(\cos x)=-\sin x\cos(\cos x).}
$$

= 9
{parent=Paper 1}
